@page "/guide"

<PageTitle>C07 · Session Outcomes and Stop Reasons</PageTitle>

<main class="student-shell">
    <div class="student-brand"><a href="/">How <span>Claude Managed Agents</span> Works</a><span class="student-badge">CONCEPT 07 / 60</span></div>
    <div class="student-hero">
        <div>
            <div class="student-eyebrow">STUDENT APPLICATION GUIDE</div>
            <h1>Session Outcomes and Stop Reasons</h1>
            <p>Understand the concepts, follow the source code, and verify the application yourself.</p>
        </div>
        <img src="astronaut.png" alt="">
    </div>
    <StudentNav />

    <section id="learning" class="student-section">
        <h2>What you will learn</h2>
        <div class="student-cards">
            <article class="student-card"><h3><span class="student-number">1</span>Idle is not always completed</h3><p>An idle session carries a stop reason. Only <code>end_turn</code> without an interruption is a completed turn.</p></article>
            <article class="student-card"><h3><span class="student-number">2</span>Classify pauses, termination and incomplete streams</h3><p><code>requires_action</code> and <code>budget_reached</code> are pauses, termination needs investigation, and a stream that ends early is incomplete.</p></article>
            <article class="student-card"><h3><span class="student-number">3</span>Keep event evidence alongside an answer</h3><p>The lab shows every observed event type next to the answer, so you can check the outcome against the evidence.</p></article>
        </div>
        <p class="student-note">Runs a real session and classifies its observed stop reason. The sample displays pauses; it does not implement approvals, resume or remote interrupt cleanup.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="run-guide" class="student-section">
        <h2>How to run this application</h2>
        <article class="student-step">
            <h3><span class="student-number">1</span>Install the .NET 10 SDK and open the application folder</h3>
            <p>From the <code>lesson-c07-csharp-app</code> folder, restore the locked dependencies (including the <code>Anthropic</code> 13.3.0 NuGet package).</p>
            <pre><code class="language-powershell">dotnet --version
dotnet restore</code></pre>
        </article>
        <article class="student-step">
            <h3><span class="student-number">2</span>Create your local .env file</h3>
            <p>Use your own Anthropic API key and an existing agent ID and environment ID. Copy the example and edit the new file in your editor. The real .env is ignored by Git.</p>
            <pre><code class="language-powershell">Copy-Item .env.example .env
notepad .env</code></pre>
        </article>
        <article class="student-step">
            <h3><span class="student-number">3</span>Prepare resources or choose the local path</h3>
            <p>For the optional live path, set your API key, then run the setup command if you do not already have resource IDs. It creates the environment before a text-only agent, saves each ID immediately, and reuses IDs already configured. It uses CLAUDE_MODEL or the source default; choose a model available to your account. An uncertain network failure may have created a resource: inspect your account before retrying.</p>
            <pre><code class="language-powershell">dotnet run --project src/LessonC07.App -- setup</code></pre>
        </article>
        <article class="student-step">
            <h3><span class="student-number">4</span>Start the application</h3>
            <p>Run the command below and wait for the printed server URL. Open <code>http://127.0.0.1:3007</code>. The terminal stays open while the server is running. If PORT differs, use that value instead.</p>
            <pre><code class="language-powershell">dotnet run --project src/LessonC07.App</code></pre>
        </article>
        <article class="student-step">
            <h3><span class="student-number">5</span>Run and inspect the evidence</h3>
            <p>Open the lab, read the stated resource operation, and press the main Run button once. Inspect the returned session ID, stop reason and events. Each live run creates a remote session.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="student-step">
            <h3><span class="student-number">6</span>Verify and stop</h3>
            <p>Run the unit tests below in a second terminal. Stop the web server with Ctrl+C. Closing a browser tab stops observing but does not confirm remote cancellation.</p>
            <pre><code class="language-powershell">dotnet test</code></pre>
        </article>
    </section>

    <section class="student-section">
        <h2>Create and understand .env</h2>
        <p>Copy the example rather than renaming it. Put your own values in .env; leave .env.example safe for sharing. Restart the server after changing configuration. PORT controls the local URL. An empty optional model value uses the source default. Real environment variables take precedence over .env values.</p>
        <pre><code class="language-dotenv">ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_api_key
CLAUDE_MANAGED_AGENT_ID=your_agent_id
CLAUDE_MANAGED_ENVIRONMENT_ID=your_environment_id
PORT=3007</code></pre>
        <p>The image below is rendered from a sanitized copy of a local file. All values except PORT are removed.</p>
        <img class="student-env" src="env-redacted.png" alt="Sanitized local .env configuration; secret values and resource IDs redacted">
    </section>
    <footer>LESSON C07 · LEARN → CONFIGURE → RUN → VERIFY<p><a href="guide#learning">Learning goals</a> · <a href="guide#run-guide">Run instructions</a> · <a href="architecture">Workflow</a> · <a href="/#application-lab">Lab</a></p></footer>
</main>
